      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The income-based system, when implemented correctly, is the most equitable because it directly addresses the fundamental injustice of housing scarcity for the most vulnerable. While the lottery offers a veneer of fairness, it ignores the reality of need, and transit prioritization only serves those who can already access those areas. Therefore, a needs-based approach is the only one that truly serves the mandate of social justice.",
      "source": "target",
